1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,944
My wrist glowed red, warning me I had only three minutes left to live, but I just kept drinking my cold morning coffee.

2
00:00:08,244 --> 00:00:18,012
People panic when their numbers drop, running into the streets like headless chickens, but I learned long ago that fighting the clock is useless.

3
00:00:18,312 --> 00:00:29,328
Every citizen gets a lifetime allotment dictated by the central registry, ticking down relentlessly until absolute zero claims your physical vessel.

4
00:00:29,628 --> 00:00:39,204
With sixty seconds left, my phone buzzed with an automated message offering final funeral arrangements, but I deleted it without a single blink.

5
00:00:39,504 --> 00:00:49,800
Thirty seconds. The digital pulse on my arm turned from a warning red to a blinding, peaceful white, signaling the final stretch.

6
00:00:50,100 --> 00:01:00,204
Ten seconds. I closed my eyes, waiting for the sudden darkness, the ultimate void that swallows everyone who reaches the end of the line.

7
00:01:00,504 --> 00:01:12,360
Zero. Instead of death, a chime echoed, and my wrist projected a bright holographic archive instead of fading into eternal blackness.

8
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:21,372
The numbers weren't counting down my life. They were counting every single second I spent refusing to look at the people who loved me.

9
00:01:21,672 --> 00:01:30,648
The timer flashed a new message in bold letters: 'Time restored. Now, spend it wisely.' My heart hammered against my ribs.

10
00:01:30,948 --> 00:01:36,036
How many seconds have you wasted waiting for your life to finally begin?
